From a67ef471a1c9cd46e9f55a20654ff218f4bda7ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:13:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] vap: mt76x02 BSS index plan + noscan so 5 GHz per-BSS
 VAPs start (W54)

The MT7612E (mt76x02) derives its hardware BSS index from byte 0 of the
vif address, so a manager BSSID plan that varies only the last byte gives
every VAP the same index and hostapd fails to open netdev 2..N with
Resource busy.  netdevs are now created on an address from the driver's
own /sys/class/ieee80211/phyN/addresses plan, the real address is reported
in 0xd00b and the manager identity stays known for later 0x6016/0x600c.

A VHT80 BSS also needs HT40, which makes hostapd run its 40 MHz
coexistence scan; on a one-channel phy that scan returns -EBUSY and the
HT20 fallback drops the VHT80 centre frequency.  noscan=1 skips only the
scan (same knob netifd uses as ht_coex=0).

The start path now waits (bounded) for AP-ENABLED and kills the instance
on timeout, so a stuck BSS can no longer hold the wiphy for the next one.
The mgmt monitor gets a free legal address on mt76x02 and is never created
on the 4-interface MT7603E.
